# In-App Access Control

JWT bootstrap: `auth-bootstrap.mdc`. Admin helpers: `lib-canonical.mdc` (`isAdmin`, `isOwner`). CRUD guard table: `business-patterns.mdc`.

**Canonical reference app:** `~/apps/jobs` — copy this pattern exactly:

| File | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `src/components/JobAccessEditor.tsx` | ACL UI — 3-segment invite picker + chips |
| `src/lib/jobAccess.ts` | Parse, expand lists, access checks, list filter |
| `src/lib/posifApi.ts` | ZAPI member/role/list helpers |
| `src/app/api/group-members`, `group-roles`, `member-lists` | Browser proxies to ZAPI |

Legacy reference (same shape): `~/apps/kanban` — `BoardAccessEditor.tsx`, `boardAccess.ts`.

Use when an app must restrict **who** can see or edit a record inside the app — by **username** (specific person), by **group role**, or by a **user list** from the space Members area.

---

## ACL UI pattern (required — do not improvise)

When a resource has private visibility, the access editor **must** expose exactly **three invite kinds** in a **3-segment control** (pill/tab toggle — one active segment at a time):

| Segment label (i18n) | Invite kind | What gets added |
|------------------------|-------------|-----------------|
| **Username** | `person` | Search members via `/api/group-members?q=`; add by `user_id` |
| **Role** | `role` | Pick from group-defined roles via `/api/group-roles`; add by `role_id` |
| **UserList** | `list` | Pick from space member lists via `/api/member-lists`; add by `list_id` |

**Selected entries render as chips** below the picker (`rounded-full` badges). Multiple chips per kind are allowed — users can add several usernames, roles, and lists on the same resource.

**Do not:**

- Replace the 3-segment control with a single dropdown, radio set, or free-text field only.
- Omit any of the three kinds (Username / Role / UserList) when `visibility === 'private'` in a Shared (space) app.
- Use JWT `role_type` buckets (`"1"`/`"2"`/`"3"`) in the picker — ACL roles are **group-defined** `role_id` values from ZAPI `/roles`.
- Show role/list pickers in personal context (`group_id === "0"`) — people-only there.

Copy `JobAccessEditor.tsx` structure: `inviteKind` state `'person' | 'role' | 'list'`, segment buttons, conditional picker panel, chip row for `memberLabels` + `roleLabels` + `listLabels`.

### Owner / admin bypass (do not add to chips)

**Space owners and admins (`isAdmin(user)` — JWT `role_type` `"1"` or `"2"`) always have full access.** They do **not** need to appear in `allowedUserIds`, `allowedRoleIds`, or `allowedListIds`, and must **not** be required in the chip list UI.

Enforce on the server in every access check and list filter:

```typescript
if (isAdmin(user)) return true   // or: skip ACL $or in buildXxxListFilter
```

The **resource creator** (`created_by` / `createdBy`) also always has access; auto-include their `user_id` in `allowedUserIds` on save if missing (`parseJobAccessInput` in `jobAccess.ts`) — but still **do not** require owners/admins in the picker.

Personal context: no role/list segments; creator + `allowedUserIds` only.

Personal **storage** (`personalDb()`) is owner-only — inviting people does **not** open the owner's bucket to them. Shared personal records need a publisher share index (`personal-storage.mdc`). Do not authorize personal rows with `isAdmin` / space roles.

## Out of scope — catalog Access Settings

**Do not implement catalog visibility in app code.** The VTC shell controls which apps appear in the catalog and who can open them (platform `app_visibility` / publisher Access Settings). That gate runs **before** the app loads. This rule covers ACL **inside** the app only — once the user is already in.

