## ZAPI — server-side only

Base URL: `getVtcApiUrl()` (`env-development.mdc`). Auth: `Authorization: Bearer <JWT>` — **not** query `token` (ZAPI is a platform service).

Require active group: `user.group_id !== "0"`.

| Endpoint | Purpose |
|----------|---------|
| `GET /api/v1/groups/{groupId}/members?limit=&offset=&q=` | Search members; resolve display names and `user_name` |
| `GET /api/v1/groups/{groupId}/roles` | List group-defined roles (`id`, `role_name`) — admin |
| `GET /api/v1/groups/{groupId}/lists` | List member lists (`id`, `title`) — admin |
| `GET /api/v1/groups/{groupId}/lists/{listId}/members` | User IDs in one list (`content_id` per row) |

Proxy from your app’s `/api/*` routes so the browser never calls ZAPI directly. Copy from jobs `src/lib/posifApi.ts` and `/api/member-lists`, `/api/group-roles`, `/api/group-members`.

### Member search — username vs display name

ZAPI members payload may include: `user_name`, `nick_name`, `full_name`, `first_name`, `last_name`, `email`, `role_id`, `role_type`.

**Display name resolution order** (jobs/kanban convention):

```typescript
const userName =
  member.user_name?.trim() ||
  member.nick_name?.trim() ||
  member.email?.split('@')[0]?.trim() ||
  String(member.id)

const displayName =
  member.full_name?.trim() ||
  [member.first_name, member.last_name].filter(Boolean).join(' ').trim() ||
  userName ||
  member.email ||
  `User ${member.id}`
```

Use `user_name` for sort/search labels; use `id` (`user_id`) for ACL storage.

